From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] localspl: AddMonitor keeps one reference, DeleteMonitor unloads it (3573)

localspl: AddMonitor keeps one reference to the monitor, DeleteMonitor unloads it

Since 1034 a loaded monitor is held by the spooler (resident). AddMonitor still kept the reference that
monitor_load gave to the call as well, so DeleteMonitor, which drops the resident one, left the monitor loaded
under its name; a later AddMonitor of the same name then found it and succeeded without loading the DLL
(Wine's winspool.drv test expects ERROR_MOD_NOT_FOUND / ERROR_PROC_NOT_FOUND there). The call's reference is
released when the monitor is resident.
---
diff --git a/dlls/localspl/provider.c b/dlls/localspl/provider.c
index 120e539..9ce88df 100644
--- a/dlls/localspl/provider.c
+++ b/dlls/localspl/provider.c
@@ -2277,7 +2277,15 @@ static BOOL WINAPI fpAddMonitor(LPWSTR pName, DWORD Level, LPBYTE pMonitors)
                 res = FALSE;
             }
             else
+            {
+                /* a monitor that stays loaded is held by the spooler (resident); the
+                 * reference monitor_load gave to this call is not kept, so that
+                 * DeleteMonitor, which drops the resident one, unloads it */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_ADDMON_REF
+                if (pm->resident) monitor_unload(pm);
+#endif
                 SetLastError(ERROR_SUCCESS); /* Monitor installer depends on this */
+            }
         }
 
         RegCloseKey(hentry);
